   "text": "I read the molecule as a PROTAC-type degrader made of three parts joined by a linker. The SMILES below was checked by hand for validity and atom count, but I did not run it through a parser.\n\n**Fragments**\n- **Spiro-oxindole end:** a 6-chlorooxindole whose C3 is spiro-fused to a pyrrolidine. The pyrrolidine carbon next to the ring NH is itself spiro to a cyclohexane. The pyrrolidine also carries a 3-chloro-2-fluorophenyl group and a carboxamide.\n- **Linker:** the carboxamide nitrogen is bonded to a para-substituted benzene, which carries a second amide. That amide continues through NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH.\n- **Degrader end:** the linker ends on the 4-position of an isoindolin-1-one. Its ring nitrogen is bonded to a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group, the lenalidomide-type unit. The stereocentre on this piperidine is drawn with plain bonds, so I gave it no stereo label.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n\nI assigned the three pyrrolidine and spiro stereocentres from the wedges and hashes:\n- The carboxamide-bearing carbon has a hashed bond to the amide carbon.\n- The aryl-bearing carbon has a wedge to the aryl ring.\n- The oxindole spiro carbon has a wedge to the lactam C=O and a hash to the aromatic ring carbon.\n\nI worked each centre out from the drawn geometry. The resulting labels are `[C@@H]`, `[C@@]` and `[C@H]` in the SMILES below.\n\nSMILES: O=C(NCCOCCOCCNc1cccc2c1CN(C1CCC(=O)NC1=O)C2=O)c1ccc(NC(=O)[C@@H]2NC3(CCCCC3)[C@@]4(C(=O)Nc5cc(Cl)ccc45)[C@H]2c2cccc(Cl)c2F)cc1"
